# Manifest for pkg/sep2tls/gotls files that check-upstream.sh cannot verify
# by diffing against upstream crypto/tls, because they have no upstream
# counterpart (fork-only) or have deliberately diverged from it (patched).
#
# Format: type<TAB>path<TAB>sha256<TAB>upstream_sha256<TAB>note
#   type: fork-only | patched
#   path: relative to pkg/sep2tls/gotls
#   sha256: sha256sum of the file's current raw content
#   upstream_sha256: sha256sum of the upstream file at UPSTREAM_TAG in
#     check-upstream.sh, at the time the patch was recorded; "-" for
#     fork-only entries, which have no upstream file to compare. For a
#     "patched" entry this is what lets the check keep watching the
#     upstream side after the fork has deliberately diverged: if the
#     pinned upstream's copy no longer hashes to this value,
#     UPSTREAM_TAG moved past what this entry was recorded against, and
#     the run reports drift so the patch gets re-reviewed against the
#     new pin. A crypto/tls security release published while the pin
#     stays put is not caught this way; see UPSTREAM.md's manual
#     procedure.
#   note: why the file exists or diverges (free text, no tabs)
#
# To add or update a fork-only entry after changing its file:
#   sha256sum pkg/sep2tls/gotls/<path>
# and replace the sha256 column on its line (or add a new line, keeping
# the tab-separated columns; upstream_sha256 stays "-").
#
# To add or update a patched entry:
#   sha256sum pkg/sep2tls/gotls/<path>                          # -> sha256
#   sha256sum <upstream checkout>/src/crypto/tls/<path>          # -> upstream_sha256
# See UPSTREAM.md, "Recording a deliberate change".
fork-only	cipher_suites_ccm.go	ef88d036575376dd6ec10d5a43ad8d32541e76209a0ab81d58ffa89d76e44788	-	CCM-8 cipher suite registration; no upstream file
